 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nDESCRIBE statement parsing broken after recent changes\n\n#### Description\n\nThe DESCRIBE statement parser appears to have issues after some recent modifications. When parsing DESCRIBE statements, the parser seems to be encountering problems with variable scoping and unreachable code.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\n\n# Try parsing a simple DESCRIBE statement\nsql = \"DESCRIBE my_table\"\nparsed = sqlglot.parse(sql)\nprint(parsed)\n\n# Try parsing DESCRIBE with additional clauses\nsql2 = \"DESCRIBE TABLE my_table PARTITION (year=2023)\"\nparsed2 = sqlglot.parse(sql2)\nprint(parsed2)\n```\n\nThe parser should handle these DESCRIBE statements correctly, but there seems to be an issue with the internal parsing logic where variables are being referenced before assignment and some code paths are unreachable.\n</issue>\n",
